  "title": "CHAPTER 4: ECONOMY OF TAMIL NADU",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "zbsbnpn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<img alt=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/6-jBPXMoZmqaDiweO0az2sVuptpHmCeLF709y7K-a5f04nc-6HBpf20j_6yHq9nEeLoZPfXqY4aepbm96n5gbOg1TAyucp9ol9BeGl7Gh0_elVTvk5y0NmL_GA0mw4qVpRfQPtNqhRjo6I8JUytTIR9JZ6QPnCEiYcG8yN2qulxkzwONtFhGsZ40ezy_LlB9?purpose=fullsize\" src=\"/books/Guide/TamilNadu CONSTABLE/images/image_u9qf6yb.jpeg\"/>Tamil Nadu has one of the strongest state economies in India. It consistently ranks among the top three states by GDP. The state has a diversified economy with strong presence in manufacturing, services, and agriculture.",
      "id": "c5r6bt7"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbhroh9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "GDP (GSDP): Among top 3 states in India (approximately Rs. 25 lakh crore in 2023-24)",
        "Per capita income: Among the highest in India",
        "Manufacturing contributes over 25% of GSDP",
        "Export-oriented economy: Chennai is called 'Detroit of India' for auto manufacturing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9k53wfc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Agriculture employs about 20% of Tamil Nadu's workforce. Tamil Nadu is a leading producer of several crops. The Kaveri delta (Thanjavur, Tiruvarur, Nagapattinam) is the main rice-growing area, known as the 'Granary of South India.'",
      "id": "yftogw0"
    },
